          "text": "# Python experimental support for free threading¶\n",
          "start_line": 29,
          "end_line": 29
        },
        {
          "id": "line-37",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "See also\n",
          "parent_id": "line-29",
          "start_line": 37,
          "end_line": 37
        },
        {
          "id": "line-41",
          "kind": "heading",
          "text": "## Installation¶\n",
          "parent_id": "line-29",
          "start_line": 41,
          "end_line": 41
        },
        {
          "id": "line-47",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "When building CPython from source, the --disable-gil configure option should be used to build a free-threaded Python interpreter.\n",
          "parent_id": "line-41",
          "start_line": 47,
          "end_line": 47
        },
        {
          "id": "line-49",
          "kind": "heading",
          "text": "## Identifying free-threaded Python¶\n",
          "parent_id": "line-29",
          "start_line": 49,
          "end_line": 49
        },
        {
          "id": "line-51",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "To check if the current interpreter supports free-threading, python -VV and sys.version contain “experimental free-threading build”. The new sys._is_gil_enabled() function can be used to check whether the GIL is actually disabled in the running process.\n",
          "parent_id": "line-49",
          "start_line": 51,
          "end_line": 51
        },
        {
          "id": "line-55",
          "kind": "heading",
          "text": "## The global interpreter lock in free-threaded Python¶\n",
          "parent_id": "line-29",
          "start_line": 55,
          "end_line": 55
        },
        {
          "id": "line-57",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "Free-threaded builds of CPython support optionally running with the GIL enabled at runtime using the environment variable PYTHON_GIL or the command-line option -X gil.\n",
          "parent_id": "line-55",
          "start_line": 57,
          "end_line": 57
        }
      ],
